<p><b>How Many Cryptocurrencies Exist?</b></p>
<p>As of April 2025, the number of cryptocurrencies is staggering. CoinMarketCap, a leading tracker, lists over 20,000 distinct cryptocurrencies, though estimates vary. The UK&rsquo;s Financial Conduct Authority pegged the figure at over 20,000 by early 2023, and it&rsquo;s grown since. However, many are inactive, illiquid, or &ldquo;dead coins&rdquo; with no real use or value.</p>
<p><b> Why So Many?</b><br />- Low Barriers: Anyone with coding skills can create a token using platforms like Ethereum or Solana.<br />- Speculation: Pump-and-dump schemes and meme coins (e.g., Dogecoin clones) inflate the count.<br />- Innovation: Legitimate projects launch tokens for specific purposes&mdash;governance, utility, or fundraising.</p>
<p>Only a fraction&mdash;perhaps 1,000&ndash;2,000&mdash;have significant trading volume or market caps above $1 million. The rest are niche, experimental, or abandoned.</p>
